// Snippet: Once Blocks
// Pattern: old sea dog with a legendary tale. First telling is epic,
//           subsequent visits are gracefully acknowledged without a flag variable
// Features: <<once>> / <<else>> / <<endonce>> for non-repeating NPC content,
//            multiple once blocks in sequence
// Run: cargo run -p bubbles-tui -- examples/snippets/once.bub
//
// Tip: use the 'b' key (step back) to rewind and observe the <<else>> branches.

title: Start
---
<<once>>
    Pete: Ahoy there, young sailor. Pull up a barrel.
<<else>>
    Pete: You again. Good. Plenty more stories where those came from.
<<endonce>>

<<once>>
    Pete: Thirty years ago I wrestled a kraken with me bare hands.
    Pete: Eight tentacles, each one thicker than a ship's mast.
    Pete: I bit off the tip of the seventh one. Still got it somewhere.
    Pete: The kraken wept. Haven't seen one since.
<<else>>
    Pete: As I told ye before. Wrestled a kraken, bit its tentacle, it wept.
    Pete: The details don't change in the repeating.
<<endonce>>

<<once>>
    Pete: Oh, and I once sailed through a storm for forty days straight.
    Pete: Lost the mainsail on day twelve. Used me hat instead.
    Pete: Finest hat I ever owned.
<<else>>
    Pete: And the forty-day storm. Hat. You know the rest.
<<endonce>>

-> Hear another tale.
    <<jump AnotherTale>>
-> Leave Pete to his memories.
===

title: AnotherTale
---
<<once>>
    Pete: Did I mention the time I navigated by the stars with one eye closed?
    Pete: The other eye was swollen shut from a jellyfish incident.
    Pete: Arrived exactly on time. Best navigation of me career.
<<else>>
    Pete: The jellyfish navigation story. Aye, I told ye that one too.
    Pete: Memory's long when ye've got nothing better to do.
<<endonce>>

-> Back to the main tales.
    <<jump Start>>
===
